+## Usage budget: an audit never runs into the account's session limit (v4.20, operator directive 2026-10-19)
+
+The intel fires and every audit share one account's usage limit, which resets on a fixed schedule. Audits kept hitting it: the 2026-09-30 audit ran four verifier slices in parallel per iteration and paused for days on the limit, and the 2026-10-18 audit spawned nineteen sub-agents in one message (about 10.5 million sub-agent tokens) and was stopped 45 minutes in, while two make-up audits ran on the same account. The limit is shared, so the only reliable prevention is to keep each audit's draw small and never to run two at once. These rules bind every audit fire; the concurrency cap and the one-audit rule are hard limits, the other numbers are guides (operator directive 2026-09-29).
+
+1. **One audit at a time.** Phase 0 step 2b claims the audit on `main` before any sub-agent spawns, and an audit that finds another audit's live claim stands down (step 2b says how). No two audits ever verify or correct the same entries.
+2. **At most four sub-agents run at any moment.** Phase 1 and Phase 2 spawn in waves of up to four, the next wave only when a slot frees; Phase 5.7 runs one verifier at a time and never splits an iteration into parallel slices.
